course: dictionary
lesson: 564
title: Auks: seabirds of the cold north
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An auk is a bird, and the word is a noun: one auk, two auks. Auks are black and white, live in the cold northern seas, and dive underwater to catch fish. You can often find out what a new word means by looking at the words around it.
explain: «The great auk was a bird of the North Atlantic with small wings it could not fly with.» The word bird tells you an auk is an animal with feathers. The clue small wings it could not fly with tells you that the great auk could not fly. So not every auk can fly.
explain: Always check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. Does «The great auk was a black-and-white seabird of the cold northern seas» still make sense? If it does, you have found a good meaning.
fact: An auk is a black-and-white seabird of the cold northern seas.
fact: Auks dive and «fly» underwater to catch fish.
fact: Puffins, guillemots and razorbills are all kinds of auk.
fact: Auks look a little like penguins, but they live in the north and most can fly.
fact: The great auk was a big flightless auk, hunted until it became extinct about two hundred years ago.
exercise: «The great auk was a bird of the North Atlantic.» What is an auk? | A type of seaweed | A rock on the coast where birds nest | *A black-and-white seabird of the cold northern seas | A large fish that swims in warm southern seas
exercise: Which of these birds is a kind of auk? | Gull | Eagle | *Puffin | Swan
exercise: «The great auk was a big flightless auk, hunted until it became extinct.» What does extinct mean? | Able to fly very far | *No living ones are left anywhere | Sleeping in a cold cave | Very hungry
test: Where do auks live? | Warm tropical seas | Rivers in the middle of Africa | *Cold northern seas | Deep inside desert caves
test: How do auks catch fish? | By flying high and diving from the sky | By hunting on land | Using a net on the beach | *By diving and swimming underwater
exam: «The last known pair was killed in Iceland in 1844.» Which bird does this sentence describe? | A puffin | A penguin from the south | *The great auk | A gull
